  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find the equations of the tangent and normal to each curve at the point where $x=1$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=(5x-4)^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Tangent: $y=20x-19$.\n\nNormal: $y=-\\dfrac{x}{20}+\\dfrac{21}{20}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y(1)&=(5-4)^4=1\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=4(5x-4)^3\\times5\\\\&=20(5x-4)^3\\\\m_{\\mathrm{tangent}}&=20(5-4)^3=20\\end{align*}$$\nTangent through $(1,1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=20(x-1)\\\\y&=20x-19\\end{align*}$$\nThe normal gradient is $-\\dfrac{1}{20}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=-\\frac{1}{20}(x-1)\\\\y&=-\\frac{x}{20}+\\frac{21}{20}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=(x^2+1)^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Tangent: $y=24x-16$.\n\nNormal: $y=-\\dfrac{x}{24}+\\dfrac{193}{24}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y(1)&=(1^2+1)^3=8\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=3(x^2+1)^2\\times2x\\\\&=6x(x^2+1)^2\\\\m_{\\mathrm{tangent}}&=6(1)(1^2+1)^2=24\\end{align*}$$\nTangent through $(1,8)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-8&=24(x-1)\\\\y&=24x-16\\end{align*}$$\nThe normal gradient is $-\\dfrac{1}{24}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-8&=-\\frac{1}{24}(x-1)\\\\y&=-\\frac{x}{24}+\\frac{193}{24}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
